// HF18 / VIZ 4.4.0: a timeout vote names the BLOCK whose QC it saw, not only the round.
//
// Before this fork the digest a validator signs when it gives up on round r carried
// (round, high_qc_round). A round is a slot, not a block: two different blocks of the same
// round produce the same high_qc_round, so a timeout certificate assembled from those votes
// did not prove that its voters had certified ONE block — only that they agreed on a number.
// The TC validity rule in validate_block_qc() could check no more than "every vote's round is
// at or below the parent QC's round".
//
// HF18 appends high_qc_block_id (20 bytes) to the vote and moves the signature to a new
// domain, viz-block-timeout-v2. A vote now says "the highest QC I hold is the QC of THIS
// block at THIS round", and the TC is only valid next to the parent QC of exactly that block:
//
//   * block_timeout_digest_v2(chain_id, round, high_qc_round, high_qc_block_id) is signed;
//   * block_timeout_vote_v2 carries high_qc_block_id; the v1 type remains unchanged;
//   * a TC includes votes below the parent QC round, and at that round only votes naming
//     the parent QC block. A validator that is behind can therefore still join;
//   * validate_block_qc enforces these same compatibility rules for every TC vote.
//   * the local vote journal gains a fifth field (the block id) and still reads pre-fork
//     four-field lines: they are verified with the v1 digest and can never join a post-fork TC.
//
// Wire compatibility: the digest and the P2P message both change, so nodes on 4.3.x cannot
// verify votes from 4.4.x nodes and vice versa. Activation needs the production 17/21
// version-vote quorum, exactly like HF16; before that the old digest is used, so an upgraded
// node on a pre-HF18 chain behaves like a 4.3.x node.
// Upgrade every node, not only validators, before 2026-11-16 00:00 UTC: older nodes cannot
// parse the new block extension.
//
// No state migration and no schema change: timeout votes live in node-local memory and the
// journal (a cache), never in chainbase. CHAIN_SCHEMA_VERSION stays 16, so an upgrade does
// not need a replay or a snapshot import.
//
// Activation: CHAIN_HARDFORK_18_TIME is a FUTURE date on purpose — unlike HF17 (a recovery
// rule whose announcement was the decision itself), this fork changes what validators sign.
// It must be announced before the moment it names, and the value changes together with the
// announcement text, never after one is published. Change it only while no announcement
// carrying this date exists.
//
// Decision: owner question #3413, answer A (2026-11-02): «мерж сейчас, активация 16.11.2026
// 00:00 UTC — как в 18.hf». The date below is therefore the announced one, and the merge of
// the PR carrying this file is the announcement; it is no longer a draft value.
#ifndef CHAIN_HARDFORK_18
#define CHAIN_HARDFORK_18 18
#define CHAIN_HARDFORK_18_TIME 1794787200      // 2026-11-16 00:00:00 UTC — announce before it names
#define CHAIN_HARDFORK_18_VERSION hardfork_version( version(4, 4, 0) )
#endif
